A rename's @from without its @drop: the old column would still go, and
only a @drop says that on purpose. Refused, the database unchanged.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup');

== after
-- @release 1
-- @from 1 column dish name = title
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== error
column `dish.title` is in the database, not in schema.sql: its values would go. Keep it, or drop it on purpose: `-- @drop 1 column dish title` in schema.sql. Renamed? Drop it, and fill the new one from it: `-- @from 1 column dish <new> = "title"`.
